MFA shorts: animated character hook (social/shorts_characters.py)

Apply from the repo root:   git apply social/shorts/CHARACTERS-INTEGRATION.patch
Needs once per machine:     pip install pycairo --break-system-packages
Then add to a spec, e.g.:   "character": {"name": "artist", "scene": "hook", "position": "lower", "corner_after": true}
  names: artist, student (F-1), worker (H-1B), owner, driver, mascot-thumbs, mascot-hmm, mascot-wow
  "corner": "mascot-thumbs" puts the mascot (not the same character) in the corner on later scenes.
What it changes: the hook text box moves above (or below) the character and the hook font drops to 108 px;
each frame is screenshotted as before and the character is pasted on in Python. Later scenes show it small in
the bottom-left corner only where the text leaves room (measured per scene, never over text). The existing
safe-area / empty-frame checks still run unchanged, plus one more: hook text must clear the character box.
Specs without "character" render exactly as before. Render time: about +35 ms per frame while a character is on
screen (roughly +20-30 s on a 25 s short).

